## Context

The spec mandates `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MMZ` (UTC, Z-suffix) in log lines. `new.go` and `log.go` both
call `time.Now().UTC()` before formatting, which is correct. `test_log.sh` already checks that a
log line matches `[0-9]{2}Z <author>`, which would catch `.UTC()` → `time.Now()` regression
(Go formats local time as `2006-01-02T15:04-0700`, no `Z`).

The remaining gap is format-precision, not timezone correctness: the existing regex `[0-9]{2}Z`
would pass if erg emitted `15:04:05Z` (with seconds) or `15:04+00:00` (offset-instead-of-Z). No
test pins the exact format `HH:MMZ` with no seconds and literal `Z` (not `+00:00`). A `TZ=`
override test documents the intent and catches that specific regression class.

## What to test

Run `erg log` under a non-UTC timezone and check the exact format:

```sh
TZ=America/Los_Angeles $ERG log TICKET "author note tz-check" "$DIR"
grep "T[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]Z " "$TICKET_FILE"   # must end in Z, not -0700
```

Also check `erg new`'s `Created:` header — it's date-only (`2026-05-30`), so timezone only matters
for the boundary between days. Verify `TZ=Pacific/Auckland $ERG new ...` produces the correct
date-only `Created:` line (no time component, no offset suffix).

Negative control: assert that a line containing `-0700` (local offset) does NOT match the Z
pattern — proving the regex is not vacuously broad.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `test_log.sh` extended: `TZ=America/Los_Angeles erg log ...` and assert log line matches
      `T[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]Z ` (exactly `HH:MMZ`, no seconds, literal `Z` not `+00:00`)
- [ ] Negative control: assert a synthetic local-offset string (e.g. `2026-05-30T10:30-0700 author note`)
      does NOT match the same pattern — proves the regex discriminates
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Notes

Drop the `test_new.sh` TZ= test: Go's `.UTC()` is applied before the `"2006-01-02"` format string,
which has no time component. The `TZ` env var is irrelevant to the output; the test would always
pass even with a broken implementation, and no regression could emit a timezone offset in a
date-only field. Not worth adding.

Do not assert the exact time value. Assert the format only: `HH:MMZ` with no seconds and literal `Z`.
